Wait: base `.joystick-pad{display:none}` later overrides earlier `display:none` and also the line-4 `.joystick-pad{display:grid}` (same specificity, later wins). Good. But `.touch-ui .joystick-pad{display:grid}` higher specificity.

Also the joystick base `inset:12px` with pad 112 → base 88. For 100 pad, inset 10 → 80, knob 42, limit 24.8.

Telemetry centering: current mobile rule `.telemetry{left:auto;right:10px;transform:none;bottom:12px...}`. My later `.touch-ui .telemetry` has higher specificity → overrides. Good. But non-touch narrow windows keep the right placement.

Also the joystick pads z-index 5; modal backdrop z-index probably higher. Check `.modal-backdrop` z-index. Let me grep. Also rails z-index. If pads z-index 5 above rails (z-index 2), they'd block rail corners. But rails are shifted up. On tablets, `.touch-ui .left-rail{bottom:158px}` and right rail max-height — pads at corners below. Good. But the left-foot is inside left rail bottom; shifting bottom up moves it above joystick. Fine, keep.

Need to check `.left-rail` base bottom value to know shift. Base likely bottom:26px. With 158 → 132px up. Joystick 112 + bottom 28 = top at 140 from bottom. So rail ends at 158 from bottom, 18px gap. Good.

For 560: joystick 100 + bottom 18 = 118 top from bottom; rail bottom 130 → 12px gap. Good.

Right rail: base top 68/94; max-height calc(100vh - 160px) on 560 → ends at top 94 + (h-160) = h-66, i.e., 66px from bottom. With joystick top 118 from bottom, overlap. My override max-height calc(100vh - 240px) → ends at 94 + h - 240 = h - 146 → 146px from bottom, 28px above joystick top (118). Good.

For touch tablets at 800px: `.touch-ui .right-rail{max-height:calc(100vh - 258px)}` with top 68 → ends at h-190 → 190 from bottom; joystick top = 28+112=140. Good gap.

