Also, why couldn't they open it again? With toggle, if ghost click or double tap toggles twice → closed and then state desync? Toggle would just flip; not prevent reopening. With explicit add, always opens.

Let me also consider `byId('spawnBtn')` on mobile is inside the left rail, which might be under the joystick pad if the rail isn't shifted (before my CSS). With pads z-index 5 covering the spawn button, tapping the spawn button actually hits the joystick pad → nothing/joystick, which could explain "can't open it again"! Yes — the pad overlay covers the button. Fixing layout solves it.

Wait, the pads were at bottom 28, left 18, 112 tall → occupy y from bottom 28..140. The spawn button sits near the bottom of the left rail (rail bottom 56). The button is roughly at y from bottom 56..94 → inside the pad zone, and pad is above (z-index 5) → taps on the button hit the pad. That's very likely the real cause of "can't open it again"! And "closes immediately" — hmm, maybe the first open came from the F key? No, on phone. Or the tap on the pad did nothing, so the modal never opened. But they said it closes immediately. Could be both: the modal opened via a tap on the edge, then a subsequent tap on the spawn area hit the backdrop → closed. Either way, layout + no backdrop close fixes it.

Good, this diagnosis is solid. Let me implement.

